##### 1. Export, including the ConfigMap the profile names  [06:59:32]
Live on your management cluster: kyverno-policies. Each variant's profile deploys the same add-ons to the same cluster, and Sveltos lets one profile manage a release at a time, so the per-cluster profiles wait until the live one steps aside. apply also writes takeover.sh, which hands each release over without reinstalling it; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.

Fix these before apply:
  - kyverno-policies names ConfigMap default/kyverno-policies in policyRefs, which is not in the input; save it with kubectl get configmap -n default kyverno-policies -o yaml > kyverno-policies.yaml and pass that file too
Onboarding plan: 1 profile over 2 clusters, one variant per cluster per profile (2 variants).
Nothing has changed. This is what ConfigHub would hold.

